From 487e684f4915f8c88adea3613b1924177fb5d338 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:22:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/39] Cut engine memory traffic on real boards (snapshots
 cg10-cg15)

- allocator: stagger large arrays by sub-page offsets so equal-size field
  arrays stop sharing cache sets (0.2-0.3 Mcell models ran 3-4x slower)
- UPML: scalar SSE path with line hooks for PML boxes that are not full-z
  slabs; compressed coefficient tables (distinct sets + per-cell index)
  on both the scalar and the f4vector path
- dispersive / Lorentz extensions: GetUsedHooks and line hooks so lossy
  boards (conducting sheets) run the fused sweep
- compressed engine: per-operator packed coefficient entries in access
  order (1-2 cache lines per operator instead of six)
- multithreaded engine: OPENEMS_FUSED_BLOCK knob (default 1, wider blocks
  measured slower), engine threads at QOS_CLASS_USER_INITIATED on macOS
- operator: thread cache key includes the first/last primitive, SetupCSXGrid
  clears the tabulated deltas; FD dumps: no PostProcess when disabled

All verified bit-identical to stock on six models (tutorials, Kirchhoff
GCPW line and SMA launch), a Drude/Lorentz box, a six-sided PML model and
the cylindrical multigrid. GCPW 4 threads 299 -> 1736 MC/s, SMA launch
437 -> 1240 MC/s (8 threads 1409).

